title: 'pallet-revive: add `burn` to the System precompile'
doc:
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    The System precompile gains `burn(uint256 amount)`. It removes `amount`, in the unit of
    `msg.value`, from the spendable balance of the calling contract or account and from the total
    issuance. Held and frozen funds and the existential deposit are not spendable. When `amount`
    has a dust part the caller does not hold, one more spendable unit is converted into dust
    first.

    The call reverts when the spendable balance of the caller is lower than `amount`, when
    `amount` is larger than the balance type of the chain can hold, when `msg.value` is not
    zero, or when the precompile is reached through a delegate call. In a static context it
    fails without revert data.

    The whole units of `amount` are reported as `Balances::Burned`, as zero for a burn of only
    dust. A dust conversion reports its own `Burned` of one unit first. No EVM log is emitted.
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Contracts can now reduce the total issuance. `System.burn` bypasses `Config::OnBurn`, which
    keeps receiving the gas rounding only, and a runtime cannot disable the function. No
    migration is needed.

    `WeightInfo` gains the required method `burn`. A runtime with its own `pallet_revive`
    weights has to re-run the benchmarks. `ISystemCalls` in `pallet-revive-uapi` gains a `burn`
    variant.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: major
- name: pallet-revive-uapi
  bump: major
- name: pallet-revive-fixtures
  bump: minor
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
